From 342d7652927f0ae6c1b45ba3bb3a57633cdeceb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:29:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] dt-bindings: clock: add the Hi3798MV100 CRG ids

The Hi3798MV100 CRG instances have no published ids. Add the per-SoC
clock id headers for the core CRG and the system controller, numbered in
(register offset, field low bit) order over every clock field the
register descriptions name and append-only, so describing another clock
later adds a table entry and renumbers nothing. The display and GPU
enables that have no documented rate are bit groups rather than gates
with a parent, consumed only to keep a block clocked while its reset
request is pulsed, and the soft resets in the same words need no ids
because they travel through the reset controller's (offset, bit) cells.
Publish the ids the Hi3798MV100 clock driver and the board files
consume.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 .../clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-crg.h         | 245 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-sysctrl.h     |  18 ++
 2 files changed, 263 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-crg.h
 create mode 100644 include/dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-sysctrl.h

--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-crg.h
@@ -0,0 +1,245 @@
